<article class="env-lemma" id="014A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/014A">Lemma <span data-tag="014A">13.4.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{D}$ be a pre-triangulated category. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (a, b, c) : (X, Y, Z, f, g, h) \to (X', Y', Z', f', g', h')  \]
</div>
  <p> be a morphism of distinguished triangles. If two among $a, b, c$ are isomorphisms so is the third. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume that $a$ and $c$ are isomorphisms. For any object $W$ of $\mathcal{D}$ write $H_ W( - ) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _\mathcal {D}(W, -)$. Then we get a commutative diagram of abelian groups 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ H_ W(Z[-1]) \ar[r] \ar[d] &  H_ W(X) \ar[r] \ar[d] &  H_ W(Y) \ar[r] \ar[d] &  H_ W(Z) \ar[r] \ar[d] &  H_ W(X[1]) \ar[d] \\  H_ W(Z'[-1]) \ar[r] &  H_ W(X') \ar[r] &  H_ W(Y') \ar[r] &  H_ W(Z') \ar[r] &  H_ W(X'[1]) }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       By assumption the right two and left two vertical arrows are bijective. As $H_ W$ is homological by Lemma <a href="/tag/0149" data-tag="0149">13.4.2</a> and the five lemma (Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/05QB" data-tag="05QB">12.5.20</a>) it follows that the middle vertical arrow is an isomorphism. Hence by Yoneda's lemma, see Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/001P" data-tag="001P">4.3.5</a> we see that $b$ is an isomorphism. This implies the other cases by rotating (using TR2). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>